    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nNumeric values in `:set` commands are never highlighted as `@number`. The `#lua-match?` pattern uses a regexp-style optional group, but Lua patterns have no such operator, so the `?` following `)` is matched literally and the pattern only accepts text like \"4.5?\".\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nUse a valid Lua pattern that accepts an integer with an optional fractional part.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-09T07:26:49Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41803#discussion_r3965649910"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/41803"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3965649910"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "This pattern, however, incorrectly highlights digits with a single trailing dot (`1.` or `123.`) as numbers. Since Lua patterns cannot express an optional group, to address this we can either switch back to `#match` or introduce a mutually exclusive second pattern:\n \n```suggestion\n  (#lua-match? @number \"^%d+$\"))\n\n((set_value) @number\n  (#lua-match? @number \"^%d+%.%d+$\"))\n```\n\nOr we can leave it as is 🤷‍♂️ ",
            "commit_id": "ca2acf7d6453fa94f899ff96c183dd77785c4610",
            "created_at": "2026-09-09T07:13:23Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -348,7 +348,7 @@\n \n ; Options\n ((set_value) @number\n-  (#lua-match? @number \"^[%d]+(%.[%d]+)?$\"))\n+  (#lua-match? @number \"^%d+%.?%d*$\"))",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41803#discussion_r3965649910",
            "id": 3965649910,
            "line": 351,
            "node_id": "PRRC_kwDOAPphoM7sXwP2",
